upplementary-material><sec id="s5a"><title>Accession Numbers</title><p>Accession numbers for gene sequences produced by this study and deposited in GenBank (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Genbank/index.html">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Genbank/index.html</ext-link>) are EU030965&#x02013;EU030988. The accession numbers of gene sequences that were not generated by this study, but were used for the analysis of the complete genome of the H7N3 viruses and the HA gene of the H16N3 viruses, can be found in <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="ppat-0030167-st006">Table S6</xref>.</p></sec></sec></body><back><ack><p>We thank Heather Forrest for excellent technical support, Hui-Ling Yen for valuable assistance in the construction of phylogenetic trees, Carol Walsh and Alice Herren for manuscript preparation, and David Galloway for editorial assistance.</p></ack><glossary><title>Abbreviations</title><def-list><def-item><term>HA</term><def><p>hemagglutinin</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>HI</term><def><p>hemagglutination inhibition</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>HP</term><def><p>highly pathogenic</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>NA</term><def><p>neuraminidase</p></def></def-item></def-list></glossary><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="ppat-0030167-b001"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hinshaw</surname><given-names>VS</given-names></name><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Turner</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1980</year><article-title>The perpetuation of orthomyxoviruses and paramyxoviruses in Canadian waterfowl</article-title><source>Can J Microbiol</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>622</fpage><lpage>629</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7397605</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030167-b002"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><n